          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b095511cd0526424b17339e769b60e388146e166",
          "message": "test(proof-methods): tamper checks for both Noir openings and a gate-count script (#6816)\n\n* test(proof-methods): tamper checks for both Noir openings and a gate-count script\n\ntamper.py now takes the circuit to check. For the Noir circuits it changes\noutputs of unconstrained hints, sampled per hint function (the rotation and\ncarry hints, the compiler's division and inverse hints), skipping an\nis-zero inverse whose input is zero, which the check leaves free by design.\ngates.sh prints each circuit's UltraHonk gate count as JSON lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015CB7XiW3NDsggNCuDcuJJo\n\n* docs(proof-methods): describe tamper.py as a smoke test; syntax-check gates.sh\n\ntamper.py changes one witness without re-solving its dependents, so a\nrejection does not show the hint's own constraints are complete. Say so in\nthe script and README. bash -n parses only its first operand, so check\nrun.sh and gates.sh separately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015CB7XiW3NDsggNCuDcuJJo\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
