          "distinct": true,
          "id": "839c07fe34d366f155add8b5745ac7902d8a2f5e",
          "message": "refactor(shacl): one JS report renderer instead of two wasm copies (#6856)\n\n* refactor(core): one JSON string escaper for every hand-written serialiser\n\nEight crates each carried a copy of a JSON string escaper (engine results\nand explain, serve change stream, wrapper, three wasm bundles, substrate).\nThey now share sparq_core::json::{escape_into, push_string}, the engine's\nrun-copying byte-level version. sparq-jsonld keeps its own because it has\nno sparq-core dependency; sparq-shacl and sparq-crdt keep theirs because\nthey escape differently on purpose (report format, JCS).\n\nOutput change: U+0008 and U+000C now encode as \\u0008 / \\u000c in the serve\nchange stream and wrapper output (previously \\b / \\f); both are the same\nJSON string. substrate's escaper now also escapes control characters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NF9xiYWvhe9DPEd3sr8neE\n\n* refactor(shacl): one JS report renderer instead of two wasm copies\n\nsparq-wasm and sparq-shacl-wasm each hand-rolled the same compact SHACL\nreport JSON (report_to_json, push_field, result_message). It now lives once\nas ValidationReport::to_js_json, with ValidationResult::message_text for the\nmessage choice that to_text and to_json also used. Output is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NF9xiYWvhe9DPEd3sr8neE\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-13T08:22:20Z",
